From ff2785db59a175492d1c7d50dcbc568ea89a5886 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tobias <ruck.tobias@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 21 Nov 2024 19:35:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [DogeCash] Parallelize PoW check (#62)

On Dogecoin, the PoW check is very expensive, which slows down the (on Bitcoin, quite fast) header pre-sync and sync.

Instead of running PoW checks sequentially, we run them in parallel using the same worker queue as for the script checks.

Current-ABC adaptation: worker queues now own their threads via RAII. Place
an independent PoW queue in ChainstateManager instead of restoring global
startup/shutdown hooks. Use the current optional-error queue interface;
keep the sequential public helper for callers and as a test oracle. Network
header validation uses the node-owned queue, without touching validation
signals or node shutdown ordering. Parameters outlive the synchronous batch.

Add real Scrypt header regression coverage for empty batches, valid batches
larger than the queue batch size, failed batches and recovery, using both
zero and two worker threads. AuxPoW checks use the unchanged verifier.

Original-Commit: 5ec37db12d4e7a9cdfbe3fcc6a5ae18e545581f6
Adapted-From: Tobias's Doged parallel PoW implementation

